    "visualDiagram": "<div class=\"visual-diagram-box\">\n            <div class=\"diagram-header-label\">\ud83c\udf10 Visual Architecture Flow: Business Capability Partitioning</div>\n            <div class=\"flow-chain\">\n              <div class=\"flow-step-node node-blue\" style=\"min-width: 180px;\">\n                <span class=\"node-label\">Enterprise Capability Map</span>\n                <span class=\"node-desc\">Order, Inventory, Billing, Shipping</span>\n              </div>\n              <span class=\"flow-arrow-separator\">\u2500\u2500\u25ba</span>\n              <div class=\"flow-step-node node-purple\" style=\"min-width: 180px;\">\n                <span class=\"node-label\">Autonomous Service Bounding</span>\n                <span class=\"node-desc\">OrderService / InventoryService</span>\n              </div>\n              <span class=\"flow-arrow-separator\">\u2500\u2500\u25ba</span>\n              <div class=\"flow-step-node node-orange\" style=\"min-width: 180px;\">\n                <span class=\"node-label\">Independent Data Stores</span>\n                <span class=\"node-desc\">Order DB / Inventory DB (isolated)</span>\n              </div>\n              <span class=\"flow-arrow-separator\">\u2500\u2500\u25ba</span>\n              <div class=\"flow-step-node node-green\" style=\"min-width: 180px;\">\n                <span class=\"node-label\">Independent Delivery</span>\n                <span class=\"node-desc\">Autonomous two-pizza team deployment</span>\n              </div>\n            </div>\n          </div>",
    "internalWorking": "Business capabilities are stable business functions that generate enterprise value. Unlike technical tiers (UI, business layer, database layer), business capabilities rarely change unless the enterprise shifts its core business model. Services communicate across well-defined REST or asynchronous event contracts. Teams own the full lifecycle from requirements to production deployment (DevOps ownership).",
    "complexPart": "Distributed transactions and data fragmentation: When a single user action touches multiple capabilities (e.g. checkout requires order creation, inventory deduction, and credit card charge), atomic ACID transactions are lost. Teams must implement the Saga pattern or asynchronous eventual consistency.",
