    "visualDiagram": "<div class=\"visual-diagram-box\">\n            <div class=\"diagram-header-label\">\ud83c\udf10 Visual Architecture Flow: DDD Bounded Context Partitioning</div>\n            <div class=\"flow-chain\">\n              <div class=\"flow-step-node node-blue\" style=\"min-width: 170px;\">\n                <span class=\"node-label\">Ubiquitous Language</span>\n                <span class=\"node-desc\">Domain definitions & workflows</span>\n              </div>\n              <span class=\"flow-arrow-separator\">\u2500\u2500\u25ba</span>\n              <div class=\"flow-step-node node-purple\" style=\"min-width: 180px;\">\n                <span class=\"node-label\">Subdomain Identification</span>\n                <span class=\"node-desc\">Core (Ordering), Supporting, Generic</span>\n              </div>\n              <span class=\"flow-arrow-separator\">\u2500\u2500\u25ba</span>\n              <div class=\"flow-step-node node-orange\" style=\"min-width: 180px;\">\n                <span class=\"node-label\">Bounded Context</span>\n                <span class=\"node-desc\">OrderContext vs CustomerContext</span>\n              </div>\n              <span class=\"flow-arrow-separator\">\u2500\u2500\u25ba</span>\n              <div class=\"flow-step-node node-green\" style=\"min-width: 180px;\">\n                <span class=\"node-label\">Context Mapping</span>\n                <span class=\"node-desc\">Anti-Corruption Layer (ACL) bridge</span>\n              </div>\n            </div>\n          </div>",
    "internalWorking": "In a monolithic system, terms like 'Product' or 'Account' mean drastically different things to Sales, Billing, and Warehousing. DDD resolves this by establishing Bounded Contexts: inside the Ordering Context, 'Product' has an SKU and pricing; inside the Shipping Context, 'Product' has physical dimensions and weight. Services communicate across Context Maps via Anti-Corruption Layers (ACL).",
    "complexPart": "Boundary definition errors: Setting boundaries too small produces 'nanoservices' that cause extreme network latency and distributed transaction hell. Setting them too large creates mini-monoliths. Identifying aggregate roots and transactional consistency boundaries is critical.",
